---
title: Auth - Login Flow (POST /auth/login)
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Client
    participant Ctrl as AuthController
    participant Service as AuthService
    participant AccountModel as AccountModel (TypeORM Repository)
    participant RefreshTokenModel as RefreshTokenModel (TypeORM Repository)
    participant Util as Security Utils (bcrypt / crypto / jwt)
    participant DB as Database (SQL Server)

    note right of Client: POST /auth/login
    Client->>Ctrl: LoginDto (username, password)
    Ctrl->>Service: login(dto)
    Service->>AccountModel: findOne({ username })
    AccountModel->>DB: SELECT * FROM Accounts WHERE Username = ?
    DB-->>AccountModel: row / null
    AccountModel-->>Service: Account Entity / null
    opt Invalid account or inactive
        Service-->>Client: Throw UnauthorizedException
    end
    Service->>Util: bcrypt.compare(password, account.password)
    Util-->>Service: isMatch
    opt Password mismatch
        Service-->>Client: Throw UnauthorizedException
    end
    Service->>Util: jwtService.signAsync(payload)
    Util-->>Service: accessToken (15m)
    Service->>Util: crypto.randomBytes(40) (generateRefreshToken)
    Util-->>Service: rawRefreshToken
    Service->>Util: hashToken(rawRefreshToken) (SHA-256)
    Util-->>Service: tokenHash
    Service->>RefreshTokenModel: save(refreshToken)
    RefreshTokenModel->>DB: INSERT INTO RefreshTokens ...
    DB-->>RefreshTokenModel: persisted row
    RefreshTokenModel-->>Service: RefreshToken Entity
    Service-->>Ctrl: TokenPairDto (accessToken, refreshToken)
    Ctrl-->>Client: HTTP 200 - TokenPairDto